course: dictionary
lesson: 3084
title: Learning words: education
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Education is a word you will meet at school, in the news and in books. Its main meaning is the teaching and learning that happens at school, college and university. «Every child has rights, such as safety, education, being heard and freedom of belief.» Here education is something every child is entitled to, so it must mean schooling and learning.
explain: Education can also mean the knowledge and skills you gain from learning. «A good education» does not only mean going to school. It means you have learned things that will help you later. The words around education give the clue: good, and helpful for the future.
explain: Sometimes education names a special subject. «Physical education» is PE, and «road safety education» teaches you how to stay safe on the road. Look at the word in front of education, because it tells you which subject it is.
fact: Education means the teaching and learning that happens at school, college and university.
fact: Education can also mean the knowledge and skills a person gets from learning.
fact: «Physical education» (PE) is a special subject about physical activity and sport.
fact: «Higher education» is learning after school, at college or university.
fact: A good check is to swap in "teaching and learning" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Every child has rights, such as safety, education, being heard and freedom of belief.» What does education mean here? | A park near the school | A kind of food | A type of holiday | *Teaching and learning at school
exercise: «Our physical education lesson is on Tuesdays.» What is physical education? | Learning to read only | *A special subject about physical activity and sport | The school bus | A type of food
exercise: «She is proud of her good education.» What does education mean here? | The school building | A football match | A bus timetable | *The knowledge and skills gained from learning
test: «A minister is in charge of one area, like health or education.» What is education in this sentence? | Blue paint | A kind of hospital | A train line | *The area of teaching and learning that a minister looks after
test: Tanya says education is only for children under ten. What is the right meaning? | *Teaching and learning that goes on through school, college and university | Only learning to count | A kind of exam pen | Lessons held only at weekends
exam: «Some countries are rich and some poor for reasons like history, wars, education and resources.» Which meaning of education fits here best? | A holiday rule | *The knowledge and skills people gain from learning | A map of the world | A type of sport
